{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793351332,"nonce":"x3q6qNn4hXwsCbrILpIBPuK+BSg=","message":"Use Ashui's compile-time CSS class catalog as an input to HXX class completion.\n\nExisting data sources already provide much of the contract:\n- ashui.css.CssCompiler.compile returns compiled bytes, imports:Array\u003cString\u003e and classes:Array\u003cString\u003e from the CSS compiler manifest.\n- CompiledCss.file resolves a path relative to the calling Haxe file, passes the resulting classes to DeclaredCss.include and registers the sheet and its imports as module dependencies.\n- DeclaredCss.classes merges classes from included compiled sheets with stylesheets declared through -D ashui_css=a.css,b.css, resolving class-path/working-directory paths and registering imported dependencies.\n\nExpose/reuse this catalog through the shared completion metadata interface. Suggest authored CSS class names together with Tw utilities in applicable HXX class literals, preserving class spelling and replacing only the current token. Include classes from imported sheets and component/library sheets already declared for the project. Use the actual declared stylesheet graph rather than scanning every CSS file on disk or maintaining a second selector parser in Rayzor.\n\nKeep the contexts distinct: an authored CSS class accepted in HXX class= is not automatically valid in Tw.tw/tw, nor can it automatically take a Tw variant such as hover:. Follow Ashui's own acceptance rules.\n\nCache metadata by project configuration/defines, calling-module path resolution, stylesheet content and transitive import fingerprints, plus provider/compiler version. Reuse cached class catalogs without waiting for full Haxe indexing or rerunning the CSS compiler on every keystroke. Publish refreshed partial results on stylesheet/import changes and isolate registries between project sessions; a pending class catalog must not be treated as proof that a class is invalid.\n\nFor CSS class documentation and go-to-definition, extend the metadata with selector/rule source locations and declaration summaries: the current successful compile result exposes class names and import paths, not per-class definition spans. Keep that provenance in the Ashui CSS compiler/provider rather than guessing it from generated Haxe or reparsing embedded binary data in the LSP. This is class-name availability and CSS-rule inference; it does not turn a CSS class into a Haxe object type.\n\nAcceptance cases: classes from -D ashui_css and CompiledCss.file, nested @imports, compound/pseudo selectors and escaped class names according to Ashui's parser, duplicate names with multiple definitions, relative paths from different modules, edits/removals in imported sheets, cold/warm metadata cache restore, mixed Tw/authored-CSS literals, and no authored-CSS suggestions inside a utility-only tw call.\n\nApplies to HXX completion 6de3a2aa106ecfb461a399bce370663734b8b7fdfab3ab83fe4f2afc8bfc7825 and Tw completion 56b5e8550a868f7d1e417e221a9d5992af82450a389c6e51c43a22c3cf551ebc.","files":null}]}